## School features connected to the team game

- Automatic unpredictable bells: provisional 30–60 second quiet intervals and 10-second chases. Seven recovered belongings reduce future interval bounds toward 15–30 seconds. No timer or monster-location debug information is displayed.
- Existing authored room encounters reserve their sequence: the quiet-phase clock pauses during them, then resumes. A timed Bell takes priority over new room encounters and pickups, preventing encounter setup from teleporting the Monster mid-chase.
- Automatic chases begin at the Monster's current location using its existing public Bell API. The team's final storage-closet setup and trailing escape chase are preserved.
- School Bell sound uses an original procedural placeholder tone. Audio, red lighting, safe-room lights, and Monster mode follow the same Bell transition. Normal lighting uses subdued blue ambient and warm room lights.
- Existing three-room safe selection and navigation exclusions are retained. The integrated Bell snapshot publishes those room IDs.
- Real pickups drive pacing and visible progress. The front key cannot skip the other objectives; leaving after the final key stops the Bell/audio and shows completion.
- Full-building room lookup chooses the smallest containing room, so large overlapping lobby slabs do not hide the Nurse/Main Office. School exposes room IDs, door states, objective snapshots, stalking candidates, and reachable navigation paths.

Implementation is in `scripts/school/school_game.gd`, an integration extension of the team's scene. Player/Monster controllers, encounter scripts, team map, and original preview are unchanged from imported main commit **cddbf56**. Changes are committed and published only to **School_System**; other branches are not modified. The earlier `scenes/school_system_demo.tscn` remains an optional isolated test scene, not the default game.

## Verification and boundaries

Godot 4.7.2: Bell regression (114 transitions), foundation (48 locations / 147 collision-tested segments), room events (2 rewards), and full-game integration checks passed with zero failures. The rendered integration test also passed; the screenshot above is its actual viewport. Integration checks cover startup, all nine objectives, hidden debug data, Bell/Monster/audio transitions without teleport, safe snapshots, real pickup pressure, final-key gating, indefinite final Bell, and exit validation.

The team currently uses placeholder models. Its Player capture/respawn interface is still a scaffold and Monster does not yet emit a capture request; this integration does not invent death detection or replace another owner's controller. Complete capture/checkpoint gameplay and a Web export remain separate team work. The old graybox maze/lab simulations are retained for tests; they do not replace the team's existing Library/Lab encounters.

Timing and lighting exports in the new main scene are provisional tuning, not permanent design rules. The larger map, seven belongings, existing minimap, safe rooms, and authored encounter exceptions are preserved per Zion's October 9 instruction.

Run checks with a working Godot executable:

```text
godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/school_bell_test.gd
godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/school_foundation_test.gd
godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/school_room_events_test.gd
godot --headless --path . --script res://tests/school_demo_test.gd
```

